 "researcher_notes": "No existing row matches. Existing Bennington rows are Midcontinent Express, Midship and a cancelled Arkoma line, none to Hugo. ONE Gas announced the line on December 18, 2025. It is a 43 mile pipeline from the Bennington Natural Gas Hub to the Western Farmers Electric Cooperative Hugo Plant near Fort Towson, Oklahoma. It will be built and run by Oklahoma Natural Gas, a ONE Gas division. A trade news article says it will cost 150 to 160 million USD, ONE Gas will pay about 120 million USD, and it will carry over 100 billion cubic feet a year. Completion is planned for the third quarter of 2028 and construction starts in 2027. An Oklahoma state senate release says the line is 24 inch and that final design and right-of-way acquisition are on schedule. Cost and capacity are not staged because they are a range and a floor. Final investment decision is not stated, so FIDStatus is blank. Concrete step: public commitment with capital budget plus right-of-way work under way. Length of 69 km is above the 25 km threshold. The line is intrastate, so no federal filing is expected. State regulator filing was not found. Owner spelled ONE Gas as the sources do. No gazetteer hit. The team style tool suggests ONE Gas Inc. No route found. Tier high on three agreeing sources, though the two news items trace to the same ONE Gas announcement."
